file:core/syswords.ts | the table of Windows words: each key is the Mac line, each value its Windows line; the pane's Swedish for the shown ones is in the rows (areas sys and engines), the rest is the English text twin or goes to Claude
text:Warn or stop when too many agents run at once. | a Setting's first note; core/settingsmap.ts NOTES replaces it at load (settings.* row)
text:All your sessions together. | a Setting's first note; core/settingsmap.ts NOTES replaces it at load (settings.* row)
text:Says early when a plan window or today's share runs out. | a Setting's first note; core/settingsmap.ts NOTES replaces it at load (settings.* row)
re:^(Sunday|Monday|Tuesday|Wednesday|Thursday|Friday|Saturday)$ | stored English day names inside a time; the band and the toast say them through the rows "Sunday {time}" ... (area engines)
text:before auto-compact | the name of a checkpoint vaken makes; a stored name, shown as written
text:On Windows vaken could not make the folder, move, copy or remove the file: PowerShell did not run or said no. | an error text kept for the plain answer of a slash command
text:under $0.01 | a price said the same in Swedish
text:9 Oct 2026 | the date of the price table, shown inside the English text twin of the cost commands
text:Edit | the name of a Claude Code tool
text:computer is full | a piece of a reason that is searched for, never shown
text:Show what needs you, the plan limit and your other sessions | the slash menu description of /vaken (English)
text:Read the app usage card now: every plan limit, its reset and its pace | the slash menu description of /vaken-usage (English)
text:Help: compacting the session and every other topic, in plain words | the slash menu description of /vaken-help (English)
re:^Is now a good moment to compact the session\? | the slash menu description of /vaken-compact (English)
re:^now \| why$ | the argument hint of /vaken-compact
text:List the vaken settings, change one, or reset them | the slash menu description of /vaken-settings (English)
text:Open this session in its own window, to drag to another screen | the slash menu description of /vaken-help run popout (English)
text:Compacting the session in a moment, with what Claude keeps. Watch for the compact marker. | the plain answer of /vaken-compact now (the English text twin)
text:Pane | the name of the pane component for the engine
text:shows fewer | the picture description (alt) of the chevron; not drawn, read by no one
text:shows more | the picture description (alt) of the chevron; not drawn, read by no one
text:Pinned | the picture description (alt) of the pin; not drawn, read by no one
file:core/compactnudge.ts | the quiet note to Claude at the compact-from crossing: English by rule, never shown to the person
# ---- rows kept on purpose: the check cannot see them used, but the line is put together at run time
built:engines. | engine lines said again in the language of the draw by their shape (trFill templates), and ledger texts built from parts
built:band. | band lines built from counts and names, said by their shape
built:pane. | pane lines and ledger titles said by their English (core/ledger.ts shownTitle turns a stored title into the shown one, then tr finds the row)
built:toast. | toast lines built from names and counts
built:needs. | Needs you lines built from a name and a reason
built:cardhome. | the Home cards' lines built from counts
built:cardship. | the Ship and Context cards' lines built from counts and names
built:cardcompact. | the This session card's lines built from counts
built:cardcontext. | the Context card's lines built from sizes
built:cardcomputer. | the Computer card's lines built from numbers
built:glance. | Glance headlines built from counts
built:explain. | what-is-this lines built from a name
built:runcost. | the task run cost lines built from amounts
built:talk. | the talk lines built from a session name
built:guard.what_n_times | built from a title and a count
built:skills.all_used_this_week | the end of a Skills line built from parts
built:skills.top | the start of a Skills line built from parts
built:access.name_selected | the spoken name of a selected row, built from the name
built:truth.a_passed | built from a count
built:common.builder_model | the role label plus " model" (core/orchestra.ts)
built:common.fixer_model | the role label plus " model" (core/orchestra.ts)
built:common.researcher_model | the role label plus " model" (core/orchestra.ts)
built:common.reviewer_model | the role label plus " model" (core/orchestra.ts)
built:common.10 | a dollar choice, built as $ and a number
built:common.25 | a dollar choice
built:common.50 | a dollar choice
built:common.100 | a dollar choice
built:common.200 | a dollar choice
built:common.5_2 | a dollar choice
text:Claude Code would not have asked the person first here, so the Guard stopped it. | a note to Claude in a stopped step's reason (English, like the other Guard notes to Claude)
text:Destroying data and exposing secrets stop by default when Claude Code would not ask first (auto mode, bypass permissions or an allow rule). Where it asks, they only warn. If vaken cannot tell, they warn. A choice you make here always wins. | a line of the typed /vaken-guard answer (English)
text:Pictures at phone, iPad and desktop size: press a row on the Preview card, when it shows. | the text twin of /vaken (English by rule)
re: A word after it runs a part: [a-z, <>-]+\.$ | the slash menu description of a command, with the words that can follow it (English)
re:^[a-z<>-]+( \| [a-z<>\[\] -]+)+$ | the argument hint of a command: the words that can follow it (English)
built:settings.english | a language name in Settings, now read from the language registry (i18n/langs.ts) and said through tr
built:settings.svenska | a language name in Settings, now read from the language registry (i18n/langs.ts) and said through tr
text:Client | a type key name in ui/kit.tsx (Omit<El, 'drag' | 'Client'>), never shown
